# drivers/bluetooth/conf: Bluetooth.
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_<NAME>=y in a defconfig builds a driver into the kernel; "standard" files are always built.
# tools/hakios-config.py reads this file; docs/drivers-config.md says what each word means and how it reaches XNU.

driver BT
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.bt.c
	help    the Bluetooth half of the WCN6750: step one, a read-only look at its three pins (bt=1)

driver BT3990
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.bt3990.c
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.bthci.c
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.btsk.c
	file    iokit/Kernel/hakios.bluetooth.cpp iokitcpp
	default n
	help    the OnePlus 6T's Bluetooth (bt=N): the WCN3990's Bluetooth half on UART6, its rampatch and NVM from the phone
	help    (fw-bt/), and iOS's own bluetoothd on it through the kernel control com.apple.uart.sk.bluetooth and a Skywalk
	help    kernel pipe (hakios.bthci.c, hakios.btsk.c, hakios.bluetooth.cpp: HakiOS's MediaTek branch's way). Not with BT
	help    (the two read bt=)
